  "query_preview": "..\nKey Message 1...Unsettled weather pattern returns Wednesday \ncontinuing into the weekend.\n\nA large scale troughing pattern will move into central Canada \ncentered over the western Hudson Bay by midweek with multiple \nshortwaves passing in the flow across the northern CONUS. This will \nresult in an unsettled weather pattern developing Wednesday with \nmultiple chances for showers and thunderstorms continuing into the \nweekend. As the early week high pressure center moves off the \nAtlantic coast Wednesday, southerly flow will begin to return \nmoisture to the area ahead of a cold front that may stall across the \nGreat Lakes region late in the week. At this time, flow appears to \nbe on the weaker side limiting more robust organized convection, but \nPWAT values return towards 1.5-1.7\" that could be supportive of more \nchances for heavy rainfall.",
